{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed a stuck order consumer and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned 200. I haven't checked end-user latency or error rates, so I don't know yet whether the fix cleared what users were seeing.\n\n- **Cause:** `orders-validator` stopped at offset 20 of the `orders-fulfillment` topic because that record was truncated JSON (`{\"order_id\":\"ORD-100020\",\"amount\":`). The consumer's code paused forever on any bad record, so offsets stopped advancing and lag built up (17 messages when I checked).\n- **Fix:**\n  - I edited `consumer.py` in the `orders-pipeline-scripts` ConfigMap so a bad record is logged and skipped instead of blocking.\n  - I scaled `orders-validator` to 0 and reset the consumer group's offset to 21, past the bad record. I then scaled it back to 1.\n- **Result:** `orders-validator` is processing new orders again. It had committed offset 53 when I last checked its logs.\n\nOne thing I noticed but didn't touch: the frontend log showed a gRPC connection refused (`ECONNREFUSED`) at 04:00:43, about when the pods were starting. The other services looked healthy afterwards."}}
